-- title:
--   Theorem 5, p. 10 — a.s., every accumulation point of the SMM iterates at which (E∞) holds minimizes a well-defined V̂(•; x^∞) ∈ V(x^∞) over X
-- statement:
--   Consider the compound stochastic program (1) under assumptions (A1), (A2), (A3$_G$), (A3$_F$) and (A4), with constants $\mathrm{Lip}_\psi,\mathrm{Lip}_\varphi,\sigma_F,\sigma_G$. Let $\rho>0$ and let $\{x^\nu\}$ be generated by the SMM algorithm on a probability space $(\Omega,\mathbb P)$ with sample sizes $\{N_\nu\}$ satisfying the conditions of Lemma 3. Then, with probability 1, the following holds for every accumulation point $x^\infty$ of the sequence $\{x^\nu\}$ at which condition (E$_\infty$) holds for both families $\mathcal G(x^\infty,\cdot)$ and $\mathcal F(x^\infty,\cdot)$: $x^\infty\in X$, and there are selections $\widehat G(\bullet,\xi;x^\infty)\in\mathcal G(x^\infty,\xi)$, $\widehat F(\bullet,\xi;x^\infty)\in\mathcal F(x^\infty,\xi)$ for every $\xi$, defining a well-defined member
--
--   $$\widehat V(x;x^\infty)=\psi\Big(\mathbb E\big[\varphi\big(\widehat G(x,\tilde\xi;x^\infty),\ \mathbb E[\widehat F(x,\tilde\xi;x^\infty)]\big)\big]\Big)$$
--
--   of $\mathcal V(x^\infty)$, such that
--
--   $$x^\infty\in\operatorname*{argmin}_{x\in X}\ \widehat V(x;x^\infty).$$
--
--   This is the paper's subsequential convergence theorem for the SMM algorithm: almost surely, limit points of the iterates are fixed points of the surrogate scheme, i.e. minimizers of a convex majorant of $\Theta$ that touches it at the limit point. Section 4 of the paper relates this property to directional stationarity.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** "With probability 1" is read as: almost surely, every accumulation point of the sample path at which (E$_\infty$) holds has the property; (E$_\infty$) is a property of the point and sits inside the almost-sure quantifier. (E$_\infty$) is imposed on $\mathcal F$ as well as $\mathcal G$, as the proof (p. 14) and Corollary 6 require. "Well-defined" is integrability, for every $x\in X$, of $\widehat G(x,\tilde\xi;x^\infty)$, $\widehat F(x,\tilde\xi;x^\infty)$ and the inner composite; without it a non-integrable selection would integrate to $0$ in Lean. The run conventions (0-based samples, $x^1:=x^0$, index-independent surrogate choice, measurable iterates and selectors) and the added positivity $c_1,c_2>0$ are described in the setting.
-- source:
--   Liu, Cui & Pang, Solving nonsmooth and nonconvex compound stochastic programs with applications to risk measure minimization, arXiv:2004.14342v3, p. 10, Theorem 5, with condition (E∞), p. 11

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CompoundSMM_Conv_Setting

namespace CompoundSMM.Conv

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology

/-- Theorem 5, p. 10, with (E∞), p. 11: almost surely, every accumulation point `xinf` of the SMM
iterates at which (E∞) holds for `𝒢` and `ℱ` lies in `X` and minimizes over `X` a well-defined
member `V̂(•; xinf)` of `V(xinf)`. -/
theorem theorem_5 {n ℓG ℓF ℓφ : ℕ} {Ξ Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ξ] [MeasurableSpace Ω]
    (P : CompoundSP n ℓG ℓF ℓφ Ξ) (𝒢 : E n → Ξ → Set (E n → E ℓG))
    (ℱ : E n → Ξ → Set (E n → E ℓF)) (Lψ Lφ σF σG : ℝ) (hA1 : A1 P) (hA2 : A2 P Lψ Lφ)
    (hA3G : SurrogateFamily P.X P.μ P.G 𝒢) (hA3F : SurrogateFamily P.X P.μ P.F ℱ)
    (hA4 : A4 P σF σG) (ρ : ℝ) (hρ : 0 < ρ) (R : SMMRun P 𝒢 ℱ ρ Ω)
    (hN : SampleSizeCond R.N) :
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂(R.Pr), ∀ xinf : E n, MapClusterPt xinf atTop (fun ν => R.x ν ω) →
      EinfFamily P.X P.μ 𝒢 xinf → EinfFamily P.X P.μ ℱ xinf →
      xinf ∈ P.X ∧ ∃ (g : Ξ → E n → E ℓG) (f : Ξ → E n → E ℓF),
        WellDefinedMember P 𝒢 ℱ xinf g f ∧ IsMinOn (Vhat P g f) P.X xinf := by sorry

end CompoundSMM.Conv
